From 93c168bcb1ee5d1c58076d91e471eb93bf245f98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Toly <1397674+AnatolyRugalev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 10:39:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] blitz-paint: outlines take outline-offset and every border
 style

An outline was always drawn solid, just outside the border box:
outline-offset was ignored, and dashed, dotted, double, groove, ridge,
inset and outset outlines came out solid. An outline pulled inside its box
with a negative offset (the usual way to outline something that fills its
viewport, which would clip the outline otherwise) was drawn off screen.

The outline is now the border of a box of its own (CssBox::outline_ring):
outline-offset outside the border box, or inside it when negative, its
rounded corners grown by the offset and the width. It is drawn with the
border's own edge code, split out of draw_border as draw_border_edges, so
it takes every border style; a solid outline stays one fill. The
OutlineBox kind and outline_box, used only by the old path, are gone.

The outline is now painted after the element's content, as CSS 2.1
Appendix E paints outlines last, so that one inside the border box is not
covered by the element's own background.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
